          ":question/worked-solution": "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (the $i$ component) is zero for *every* vector. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(x,y)&=-2\\,i \\\\ H(x,y)&=5\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (the $j$ component) is positive and stays constant across the plane. Therefore, we can rule out:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-3\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $F(x,y)=4\\,j.$",
